# The ledger of `mcp`: what the Model Context Protocol's SDKs let a program
# do, one block per capability, and what Rebel answers. The protocol is the
# revision 2026-07-28, read on 2026-11-17 from the specification's own
# repository (its pages and `schema.ts`, fetched into the scratch folder),
# the newest beside `draft`. None of the three standard libraries speaks
# MCP, so the yardstick is the census the author chose on 2026-11-17,
# measured on this machine that day: Go's official
# `github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/mcp` v1.8.0 and
# `github.com/mark3labs/mcp-go` v1.5.0 (`mcp`, `server`, `client`; `go doc`,
# fetched into the scratch folder's module cache), both of which name
# 2026-07-28; Python's `mcp` 2.3.0 (`dir()`, installed into the scratch
# folder), which speaks it; and the TypeScript SDK's npm package
# `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk` 1.32.2, of which only the exports map was read
# (`client`, `server`, `validation`, `experimental/tasks`), so its entries are
# not listed name by name. No Rust SDK is on this machine: the `rust` lines
# read `-`.
#
# Measured against Python's `mcp` 2.3.0 client on 2026-11-18: the example
# server `examples-rebel/reach_mcp.hero`, built, answered every call of that
# client over standard streams and over Streamable HTTP (discovery, the four
# tools with a structured result, the program's own state, an elicitation by
# multi round-trip, `x-mcp-header` with text of more than one byte through
# the Base64 sentinel, a schema refusal as a tool error, resources, a
# template, a prompt, a completion, "Resource not found").

capability protocol/version  the revision named and every request held to it: no handshake, the version in each request's `_meta`, -32022 with the versions spoken
  heroes  mcp.PROTOCOL_VERSION, mcp.UNSUPPORTED_PROTOCOL_VERSION, mcp.handle
  go      go-sdk mcp.SupportedProtocolVersions, mcp.MetaKeyProtocolVersion, mcp-go mcp.ProtocolVersion20260728, server.FilterSupportedVersions, server.RequestProtocolVersion, server.IsModernRequest, client.WithProtocolVersion
  rust    -
  python  mcp.client.Client.protocol_version, mcp.shared.version
  note    An `initialize` is answered -32022 naming the version spoken, as the revision asks of a server that speaks it alone

capability protocol/meta  a request's `_meta` read and checked: version, client, capabilities, progress token, log level, the trace context kept
  heroes  mcp.meta_of, mcp.RequestMeta
  go      go-sdk mcp.Meta, mcp.Params.GetMeta, mcp-go server.WithRequestProtocolInfo, client.WithMetaPropagator, client.WithPropagator
  rust    -
  python  mcp.types, mcp.server.context
  note    A request missing a required field is answered -32602, and on HTTP 400, as the revision asks

capability protocol/discover  `server/discover` answered from the server's description, and asked by a client
  heroes  mcp.handle, mcp.discover, mcp.Discovered
  go      go-sdk mcp.DiscoverParams, mcp.DiscoverRequest, mcp.DiscoverResult, mcp-go server.OnAfterDiscoverFunc, client.WithDiscoverTimeout
  rust    -
  python  mcp.client.Client.server_info, server_capabilities, instructions, prior_discover

capability protocol/identity  a server's and a client's name, version, title, site and icons
  heroes  mcp.Implementation, mcp.implementation, mcp.Icon, mcp.implementation_json, mcp.implementation_of, mcp.icons_json, mcp.icons_of
  go      go-sdk mcp.Implementation, mcp.Icon, mcp.IconTheme, mcp-go mcp.Implementation
  rust    -
  python  mcp.Implementation, mcp.client.Client.client_info

capability protocol/capabilities  a client's and a server's capabilities, extensions among them, written and read
  heroes  mcp.ClientCapabilities, mcp.ServerCapabilities, mcp.form_capabilities, mcp.no_capabilities, mcp.capabilities_of, mcp.client_capabilities_json, mcp.client_capabilities_of, mcp.server_capabilities_json, mcp.server_capabilities_of
  go      go-sdk mcp.ClientCapabilities, mcp.ServerCapabilities, mcp.ElicitationCapabilities, mcp.FormElicitationCapabilities, mcp.CompletionCapabilities, mcp-go client.WithClientCapabilities
  rust    -
  python  mcp.ClientCapabilities, mcp.ServerCapabilities, mcp.ToolsCapability, mcp.ResourcesCapability, mcp.PromptsCapability, mcp.client.ClientExtension, mcp.client.advertise

capability protocol/errors  the protocol's error codes and their HTTP statuses
  heroes  mcp.HEADER_MISMATCH, mcp.MISSING_REQUIRED_CLIENT_CAPABILITY, mcp.UNSUPPORTED_PROTOCOL_VERSION, mcp.respond_http
  go      go-sdk mcp.CodeHeaderMismatch, mcp.CodeResourceNotFound, mcp.ResourceNotFoundError, mcp-go server.NewHandlerError, server.JSONRPCErrorProvider
  rust    -
  python  mcp.MCPError, mcp.types.ErrorData
  note    A resource not there is -32602, the revision's code; -32002 of the revision before is read by a client as the failure it is

capability server/description  a server described as data: its tools, resources, templates, prompts, what it tells, its pages and freshness
  heroes  mcp.Server, mcp.new_server
  go      go-sdk mcp.Server, mcp.NewServer, mcp.ServerOptions, mcp.AddTool, mcp.Server.AddPrompt, mcp.Server.AddResource, mcp.Server.AddResourceTemplate, mcp-go server.MCPServer, server.NewMCPServer, server.ServerOption
  rust    -
  python  mcp.server.MCPServer, mcp.server.Server, mcp.server.mcpserver
  note    The language has no closure, so the program describes, `handle` finds, and the program calls its own function with its own state, as `web` routes

capability server/dispatch  each request found and checked, the package answering what it can from the description, the rest handed to the program
  heroes  mcp.handle, mcp.Request, mcp.tool_named
  go      go-sdk mcp.Server.Run, mcp.ServerSession, mcp-go server.MCPServer.HandleMessage, server.Hooks and their OnAfter functions
  rust    -
  python  mcp.server.lowlevel, mcp.server.session, mcp.server.runner

capability tools/list  tools listed with the JSON Schema of their inputs, their output schema, hints and icons, in a fixed order, page by page
  heroes  mcp.Tool, mcp.new_tool, mcp.Hints, mcp.default_hints, mcp.tool_json, mcp.tool_of, mcp.list_tools
  go      go-sdk mcp.Tool, mcp.ToolAnnotations, mcp.ListToolsParams, mcp.ListToolsResult, mcp-go mcp.NewTool, mcp.WithDescription, mcp.WithString, mcp.WithNumber, mcp.ToolAnnotation
  rust    -
  python  mcp.Tool, mcp.ListToolsResult, mcp.client.Client.list_tools

capability tools/call  a tool called, its arguments held to its input schema, its result: content, structured content checked against the output schema, an execution error the model reads
  heroes  mcp.ToolCall, mcp.ToolResult, mcp.answer_tool, mcp.text_result, mcp.error_result, mcp.structured_result, mcp.tool_result_json, mcp.tool_result_of, mcp.call_tool, mcp.ToolOutcome
  go      go-sdk mcp.CallToolParams, mcp.CallToolParamsRaw, mcp.CallToolRequest, mcp.CallToolResult, mcp.ToolHandler, mcp-go mcp.CallToolResult, mcp.NewToolResultText, mcp.NewToolResultError, mcp.NewToolResultStructured
  rust    -
  python  mcp.CallToolRequest, mcp.client.Client.call_tool, mcp.server.validation
  note    Arguments the input schema refuses are a tool execution error (`isError`), so the model can correct them, as Python answers; a result that does not conform to the output schema is the program's mistake and is answered -32603

capability content  content blocks of text, image, audio, a resource link and an embedded resource, with their hints
  heroes  mcp.Content, mcp.Annotations, mcp.no_annotations, mcp.text_content, mcp.content_json, mcp.content_of, mcp.annotations_json, mcp.annotations_of
  go      go-sdk mcp.Content, mcp.TextContent, mcp.ImageContent, mcp.AudioContent, mcp.ResourceLink, mcp.EmbeddedResource, mcp.Annotations, mcp-go mcp.TextContent, mcp.ImageContent, mcp.AudioContent, mcp.EmbeddedResource
  rust    -
  python  mcp.types
  note    A block's own `_meta` is not written or read

capability resources/list-read  resources listed and read as text or bytes, cacheable as the server says
  heroes  mcp.Resource, mcp.new_resource, mcp.Contents, mcp.ResourceRead, mcp.answer_resource, mcp.resource_json, mcp.resource_of, mcp.contents_json, mcp.contents_of, mcp.list_resources, mcp.read_resource, mcp.ReadOutcome
  go      go-sdk mcp.Resource, mcp.ResourceContents, mcp.ReadResourceParams, mcp.ReadResourceResult, mcp.ListResourcesResult, mcp.ResourceHandler, mcp-go mcp.NewResource, mcp.TextResourceContents, mcp.BlobResourceContents
  rust    -
  python  mcp.Resource, mcp.ReadResourceRequest, mcp.ReadResourceResult, mcp.client.Client.list_resources, read_resource

capability resources/templates  resource templates listed, a URI matched to one and its variables read, RFC 6570 expanded
  heroes  mcp.ResourceTemplate, mcp.new_template, mcp.template_json, mcp.template_of, mcp.list_templates, mcp.expand_template, mcp.match_template
  go      go-sdk mcp.ResourceTemplate, mcp.ListResourceTemplatesResult, mcp-go mcp.NewResourceTemplate
  rust    -
  python  mcp.UriTemplate, mcp.InvalidUriTemplate, mcp.client.Client.list_resource_templates
  note    RFC 6570 has no matching; each expression takes what its operator writes up to the next literal, so a template whose expressions touch is matched as far as that reads. It belongs in `url` in the end, which holds no URI template today

capability prompts  prompts listed with their arguments and asked for, a missing argument refused
  heroes  mcp.Prompt, mcp.PromptArgument, mcp.PromptMessage, mcp.PromptResult, mcp.PromptGet, mcp.new_prompt, mcp.prompt_json, mcp.prompt_of, mcp.answer_prompt, mcp.list_prompts, mcp.get_prompt, mcp.PromptOutcome
  go      go-sdk mcp.Prompt, mcp.PromptArgument, mcp.PromptMessage, mcp.GetPromptParams, mcp.GetPromptResult, mcp-go mcp.NewPrompt, mcp.NewPromptMessage
