capability cancellation  `notifications/cancelled` read by a server on standard streams and sent by a client; over HTTP a stream closed
  heroes  mcp.Request, mcp.cancel
  go      go-sdk mcp.CancelledParams, mcp-go mcp.CancelledNotification
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    A server is single-threaded unless the program makes it otherwise, so a cancellation of the request it is answering arrives after its answer, a race the revision allows

capability subscriptions  `subscriptions/listen` acknowledged with what the server agrees to, list changes and resource updates told only where asked, the subscription ended gracefully; a client that opens one and reads its notifications
  heroes  mcp.Listen, mcp.Filter, mcp.honored_filter, mcp.acknowledge, mcp.changed_notification, mcp.updated_notification, mcp.end_listen, mcp.filter_of, mcp.filter_json, mcp.subscribe, mcp.next_notification, mcp.Notification
