capability auth/server  a protected resource's metadata served (RFC 9728), the 401 and 403 challenges written, the token read
  heroes  mcp.resource_metadata_response, mcp.unauthorized, mcp.insufficient_scope, http.bearer_token_of
  go      go-sdk auth.RequireBearerToken, auth.ProtectedResourceMetadataHandler, mcp-go server.NewProtectedResourceMetadataHandler, server.ProtectedResourceMetadataPath, server.WellKnownProtectedResourcePath
  rust    -
  python  mcp.server.auth
  note    The token is checked by the program, a JWT with `jose` or an opaque one with `oauth2.introspect`, its audience the server's canonical URL; the metadata and the challenge are `oauth2`'s, not written again

capability auth/client  a 401 read, the protected resource's and the authorization server's metadata fetched, the canonical resource and the scopes chosen, an `oauth2` client made with its resource set; the flow, PKCE, RFC 9207's `iss` and client ID metadata documents are `oauth2`'s
  heroes  mcp.Authorization, mcp.canonical_resource, mcp.discover_authorization, mcp.config_for, mcp.with_token, mcp.Client
  go      mcp-go client.NewOAuthStreamableHttpClient, client.OAuthConfig, client.AuthorizationRequiredError, client.IsAuthorizationRequiredError, client.GetResourceMetadataURL, client.GetOAuthHandler, client.ErrAuthorizationServerChanged, client.TokenStore, client.MemoryTokenStore, client.Token, client.GenerateCodeVerifier, client.GenerateCodeChallenge, client.GenerateState, go-sdk oauthex
  rust    -
  python  mcp.client.auth
  note    No token is kept between calls, as `oauth2` keeps none; a client's credentials keyed by issuer are the program's

capability client/requests  a client of one server: every request of the revision, its `_meta` written, a result's type checked, the notifications that come before an answer kept
  heroes  mcp.Client, mcp.Link, mcp.send_request, mcp.discover, mcp.list_tools, mcp.call_tool, mcp.list_resources, mcp.list_templates, mcp.read_resource, mcp.list_prompts, mcp.get_prompt, mcp.complete, mcp.next_notification
